  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Brazilian Pernambuco (Recife) carnival fast-tempo brass-band marcha tradition codified 1907-onward as the working-class-and-capoeira-defense response to the elite-elite carnival-club tradition. The canonical frevo-orquestra ensemble: trumpets, trombones, saxophones, and rhythm-section (snare-and-bass-drum military-marching kit, sometimes augmented with percussive surdo-and-tamborim Brazilian-samba percussion). The frevo-de-rua street-version is purely instrumental and very fast (typically 200+ BPM), led by passistas dancers carrying small umbrellas (sombrinhas) executing the characteristic acrobatic-jumping passo-de-frevo footwork. Three sub-genres: frevo-canção (sung-frevo with vocal-lyrics), frevo-de-bloco (more relaxed bloco-carnival-association style), and frevo-de-rua (instrumental-street-version).",
